Joeb wrote:

> This monk isn't any of those.  She's wearing studded leather armor and
> kicking to avoid the "Your armor is cumbersome" message.

The message is just that, a message.  It doesn't mean anything
directly.  What does (or may) matter is that you get a -20 to
hit bonus.  At lower experience levels, it may come into play.
A lot of things enter into the calculations, but with enough
experience/luck, you'll hit all the time even with it.  (The
only time I wore body armor as a monk, I was at XL30 and
carrying a blessed luckstone.  Off hand, without doing any real
calculations, I'd guess it would become an option somewhere
between XP10 and XP15 with a blessed luckstone.)

Similarly, you get a to hit bonus if you're not wielding a
weapon, and you're not wearing body armor or a shield.  Again,
with enough experience, you don't care.  On the other hand, as a
grand master in marial arts, you'll do enough damage so that
only a good artefact will be worth it.  (The previously
mentionned monk had a +7 Grayswandir.)

None of the penalties affect ranged weapons; I'm usually able to
find a crossbow and enough bolts to make it worth while,
especially for the monsters you don't want to approach.

